},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3529490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis","id":3529490,"login":"Caldis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Mjk0OTA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/commits/cc683dd7b1f7ac3721a19b3c6b59c11fda747be1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T10:52:03Z","email":"mail@caldis.me","name":"Caldis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T10:52:03Z","email":"mail@caldis.me","name":"Caldis"},"message":"feat(core): hotKey rotate / download + custom-descriptor surface (1.5.0)\n\nNew default hotkeys:\n- [ / ] rotate counter-/clockwise (desktop preset; on by default)\n- Mod+S download current image (desktop preset; OFF by default — opt-in\n  because enabling it hijacks the browser''s \"Save Page As\" shortcut)\n\nHotKey value type widened from boolean to HotKeyValue =\n  boolean | string | string[]\n  - true   → use library default\n  - false  → disabled (event passes through to outer listeners)\n  - string → custom descriptor: ''Escape'' / ''BracketLeft'' / ''S'' / ''Mod+S''\n             (e.code names — physical key positions, layout-independent;\n              single letters/digits short-form to KeyX/DigitX;\n              Mod prefix = ⌘ on macOS, Ctrl on Windows/Linux)\n  - string[] → multiple bindings, any matches triggers\n\nUmbrella keys (flip / rotate) stay boolean-only; per-side string descriptor\nwins over umbrella. Strict modifier matching: undeclared modifiers must NOT\nbe pressed (e.g. ''Space'' is never matched by Cmd+Space — input-method safe).\n\nInternals: replaced switch(e.keyCode) with sequential matchAnyHotKey table\nin Browser.handleKeyDown. New utils/hotkey.ts exposes parseHotKey /\nmatchHotKey / resolveHotKeyValue / resolveSideBinding (13 unit tests).\n\nTests: 153/153 (10 new integration tests cover [ / ], Cmd+S vs Ctrl+S\ncross-platform, bare-S non-trigger, Cmd+Shift+S strict-modifier rejection,\npreventDefault on Mod+S to suppress browser \"Save Page As\").\n\nDocs: HotKey API surface synced across llms.txt, README, AGENTS, home docs\n(Props.tsx + 7 i18n languages × 8 new keys), home schema defPreset mirror,\nplayground HotKeyControl, llms-eval contract (16/16 assertions).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3dd7d63e453b63337ac793d3c6494dd8da135c24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/git/trees/3dd7d63e453b63337ac793d3c6494dd8da135c24"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/git/commits/cc683dd7b1f7ac3721a19b3c6b59c11fda747be1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3529490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis","id":3529490,"login":"Caldis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Mjk0OTA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis/react-zmage/commit/cc683dd7b1f7ac3721a19b3c6b59c11fda747be1","node_id":"C_kwDOBnXMktoAKGNjNjgzZGQ3YjFmN2FjMzcyMWExOWIzYzZiNTljMTFmZGE3NDdiZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis/react-zmage/commit/fe4ae7e145c17b0f5685e2e9daf02d7f31a530bd","sha":"fe4ae7e145c17b0f5685e2e9daf02d7f31a530bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/commits/fe4ae7e145c17b0f5685e2e9daf02d7f31a530bd"}],"sha":"cc683dd7b1f7ac3721a19b3c6b59c11fda747be1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/commits/cc683dd7b1f7ac3721a19b3c6b59c11fda747be1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3529490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis","id":3529490,"login":"Caldis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Mjk0OTA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/commits/fe4ae7e145c17b0f5685e2e9daf02d7f31a530bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T09:21:14Z","email":"mail@caldis.me","name":"Caldis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T09:21:14Z","email":"mail@caldis.me","name":"Caldis"},"message":"refactor(core)!: rename closeOnDoubleClick → hideOnDblClick (BREAKING)\n\nAligns the auto-dismiss trigger family. The 1.4.0-introduced prop was\nnamed closeOnDoubleClick which broke the existing hideOn<Event> convention\n(hideOnScroll). With both props naming the same outcome (modal goes away\non a user action), a single family is clearer:\n\n  hideOnScroll   — auto-close on page scroll (desktop only)\n  hideOnDblClick — auto-close on image double-click (NEW name)\n\nAlso shorter (15 vs 18 chars) and aligns with the DOM-native event name\n(`dblclick`, `ondblclick` HTML attribute).\n\nNo deprecation alias kept: 1.4.0/1.4.1 are very recent (~days), adoption\nsurface tiny, deprecation alias would be over-engineering.\n\nReordered docs/schema so the two `hide*` props sit adjacent (per the\n\"trigger family\" mental model). Now the home schema, README tables,\nAGENTS reference, and llms.txt all show:\n\n  hideOnScroll\n  hideOnDblClick   ← (was further down as closeOnDoubleClick)\n  coverVisible\n  ...\n\nFiles touched (rename across all destinations per sync-public-docs flow):\n  - core types (global.ts InterfaceAndInteractionParams, default.ts defProp,\n    Browser.tsx context plumbing, Image.tsx handleDoubleClick consumer)\n  - core test suite (test names + JSX prop)\n  - home schema (defProp mirror + PARAM_SCHEMA reorder)\n  - 7 i18n files (en/de/es/fr/ja/ko/zh-CN), 283/283 keys parity verified\n  - README.md / README.zh-CN.md (interface table row + Full type comment)\n  - AGENTS.md (prop quick-reference Interface row + family note)\n  - llms.txt + docs/llms.txt (regenerated via home build)\n  - llms-eval contract assertion (now asserts hideOnDblClick)\n\nVerification:\n  - 112/112 core unit + integration tests pass\n  - llms-eval 16/16 static contract pass\n  - tsup build clean (ESM/CJS/SSR)\n  - pnpm -w run check: r17/r18/r19/nextjs sandboxes + 3 SSR smoke pass\n\nMigration note for any 1.4.0-1.4.1 user adopting closeOnDoubleClick:\n  Rename the prop to hideOnDblClick. Default and behavior unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bdadfbf6c7b94354039d2b2edc7e88cb46eaf57e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/git/trees/bdadfbf6c7b94354039d2b2edc7e88cb46eaf57e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/git/commits/fe4ae7e145c17b0f5685e2e9daf02d7f31a530bd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3529490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis","id":3529490,"login":"Caldis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Mjk0OTA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis/react-zmage/commit/fe4ae7e145c17b0f5685e2e9daf02d7f31a530bd","node_id":"C_kwDOBnXMktoAKGZlNGFlN2UxNDVjMTdiMGY1Njg1ZTJlOWRhZjAyZDdmMzFhNTMwYmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis/react-zmage/commit/1988bff8c02b344243a2be5960c5c67e33aed027","sha":"1988bff8c02b344243a2be5960c5c67e33aed027","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/commits/1988bff8c02b344243a2be5960c5c67e33aed027"}],"sha":"fe4ae7e145c17b0f5685e2e9daf02d7f31a530bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/commits/fe4ae7e145c17b0f5685e2e9daf02d7f31a530bd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3529490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis","id":3529490,"login":"Caldis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Mjk0OTA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/commits/1988bff8c02b344243a2be5960c5c67e33aed027/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T09:02:28Z","email":"mail@caldis.me","name":"Caldis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T09:02:28Z","email":"mail@caldis.me","name":"Caldis"},"message":"feat(core): add loadingDelay prop with anti-flicker delay-before-show\n\nLoading indicator was synchronously set on every page change and only cleared\nby a 500ms polling fallback. Cached / key-reused pages flashed the spinner\n~500ms then hid it — annoying visual noise especially when paging quickly\nthrough pre-loaded images.\n\nThree coordinated changes implement the industry-standard \"delay-before-show\"\npattern (see Ant Design Spin `delay`, react-loadable `delay`, TanStack Query):\n\n1. New public prop `loadingDelay: number` (default 200ms; range 0-1000 in\n   playground). Defers `isFetching=true` setState by N ms; if the image\n   loads within the window via any path (onLoad event, polling, or cdU\n   fast-path), the delay timer is cancelled → loading indicator never shows.\n\n2. cdU page-change fast-path: when `node.complete && naturalWidth > 0`\n   on the new center (cached image, key-reused side→center), call\n   `handleImageLoadEnd` directly. Skips loading state entirely, no timer\n   needed. Combined with the scale-calibration interrupt and canZoom\n   recompute already wired here, all three concerns now share the same\n   \"new center is ready\" branch.\n\n3. handleImageLoad (centerOnLoad path) now calls handleImageLoadEnd. Was\n   relying solely on 500ms polling to clear loading; onLoad is the canonical\n   \"image is loaded\" signal — using it directly cuts the polling-driven\n   flash window from ~500ms to one render cycle.\n\nBehavior matrix:\n  Cached page change          → no Loading shown (fast-path)\n  Fast load (<200ms)          → no Loading shown (delay timer cancelled)\n  Medium load (200-500ms)     → Loading shown 0-300ms\n  Slow load (>500ms)          → Loading shown N-200ms (vs N-500ms before)\n\nTests added (4 new, 112 total):\n  - Cached page change: #zmageLoading not in DOM throughout (fast-path lock)\n  - loadingDelay=50 prop: Loading appears around 50ms for uncached page\n  - Fast onLoad cancels delay timer: Loading never shown\n  - StrictMode unmount cancels loadingShowDelayTimer (cleanup invariant)\n\nPublic docs synced (sync-public-docs skill, all 8 destinations):\n  - types/global.ts InterfaceAndInteractionParams; defProp.loadingDelay\n  - getConfigFromProps + Browser context value (single-source plumbing)\n  - home/schema/param-schema.ts (PARAM_SCHEMA + defProp mirror)\n  - 7 i18n files (en/de/es/fr/ja/ko/zh-CN), all 283 keys parity verified\n  - README.md / README.zh-CN.md interface props table + Full type comment\n  - AGENTS.md prop quick-reference Interface row\n  - llms.txt API table row; docs/llms.txt regenerated via home build\n  - llms-eval/eval.test.mjs new contract assertion (16/16 pass)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6ec5310c272742df35d4e512de1c0c9b65515d12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/git/trees/6ec5310c272742df35d4e512de1c0c9b65515d12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/git/commits/1988bff8c02b344243a2be5960c5c67e33aed027","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3529490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis","id":3529490,"login":"Caldis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Mjk0OTA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis/react-zmage/commit/1988bff8c02b344243a2be5960c5c67e33aed027","node_id":"C_kwDOBnXMktoAKDE5ODhiZmY4YzAyYjM0NDI0M2EyYmU1OTYwYzVjNjdlMzNhZWQwMjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis/react-zmage/commit/d2834bf4605f363e17370ffc287b8492218b7b2f","sha":"d2834bf4605f363e17370ffc287b8492218b7b2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/commits/d2834bf4605f363e17370ffc287b8492218b7b2f"}],"sha":"1988bff8c02b344243a2be5960c5c67e33aed027","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/commits/1988bff8c02b344243a2be5960c5c67e33aed027"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3529490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis","id":3529490,"login":"Caldis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Mjk0OTA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/commits/d2834bf4605f363e17370ffc287b8492218b7b2f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T06:32:34Z","email":"mail@caldis.me","name":"Caldis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T06:32:34Z","email":"mail@caldis.me","name":"Caldis"},"message":"fix(core): converge canZoom recompute on page-change key-reuse path\n\nRegression introduced (or exposed) by commit 2fda167 (pagination shortest-path):\nwhen the user switches to a smaller-than-viewport image via a path that triggers\nReact key reuse (side→center, including the new shortest-path pagination flow\nfor in-pre-fetch-ring jumps like N=6 dot 0→5), the new center node''s src does\nNOT change → browser does NOT dispatch the ''load'' event → handleImageLoad does\nNOT fire → reportCanZoom is never invoked → canZoom stays at the optimistic\n`true` value that handleSwitchPages set as a placeholder.\n\nVisible symptom: zoom button does not show disabled state on a small image\nthat was reached via flip; spacebar can still trigger zoom mode incorrectly.\nResizing the window after switching corrects it (handleResize → reportCanZoom).\n\nThis is the same #167 root pattern (key-reused side becomes center, no onLoad,\nstate stale): commit 2fda167 fixed scale via debounceUpdateCurrentImageStyle\nin cdU; canZoom needed the symmetric treatment.\n\nFix: add `this.reportCanZoom()` next to the existing\ndebounceUpdateCurrentImageStyle in cdU''s page-change block. Now all three\ncanZoom triggers — handleResize, handleImageLoad, and page-change cdU —\nconverge on a single source (`reportCanZoom`), which itself reads from the\nsingle source of truth (imageRef.current.naturalWidth + viewport).\n\nreportCanZoom self-guards on naturalWidth=0, so calling on every page change\nis safe — fresh-mount uncached images no-op until handleImageLoad fires later.\n\nTests:\n- 大图→小图 key-reuse 路径: zoom button gains ''disabled'' class within 20ms\n  of the flip (was: stuck without ''disabled'' class — pre-fix bug).\n- 小图→大图 key-reuse 路径: zoom button loses ''disabled'' class symmetrically.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"93d5d8617a32e48d300e1e09213f81001c9dfc66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/git/trees/93d5d8617a32e48d300e1e09213f81001c9dfc66"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/git/commits/d2834bf4605f363e17370ffc287b8492218b7b2f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3529490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis","id":3529490,"login":"Caldis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Mjk0OTA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis/react-zmage/commit/d2834bf4605f363e17370ffc287b8492218b7b2f","node_id":"C_kwDOBnXMktoAKGQyODM0YmY0NjA1ZjM2M2UxNzM3MGZmYzI4N2I4NDkyMjE4YjdiMmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis/react-zmage/commit/a0cb1541301a040396ed23e1bbb8985d1ce59417","sha":"a0cb1541301a040396ed23e1bbb8985d1ce59417","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/commits/a0cb1541301a040396ed23e1bbb8985d1ce59417"}],"sha":"d2834bf4605f363e17370ffc287b8492218b7b2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/commits/d2834bf4605f363e17370ffc287b8492218b7b2f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3529490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis","id":3529490,"login":"Caldis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Mjk0OTA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/commits/a0cb1541301a040396ed23e1bbb8985d1ce59417/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T06:21:35Z","email":"mail@caldis.me","name":"Caldis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T06:21:35Z","email":"mail@caldis.me","name":"Caldis"},"message":"docs(methodology): complex animation/interaction debugging framework\n\nDistills the methodology used across two waves of flip-module bug fixes\n(commits 0664d82, 2fda167) into a reusable debugging framework specifically\ntuned for complex animation and interaction bugs in React/CSS systems.\n\nFramework covers:\n  - 4 core principles (visual is truth; data race over visual hack;\n    multi-role independent review with confidence calibration; reuse\n    existing patterns over inventing new mechanisms)\n  - 5-phase process (symptom capture → mechanism localization → solution\n    enumeration → red-team validation → ship + visual verification)\n  - Multi-agent collaboration template (Investigator / Solution Architect\n    / Red Team / Implementer roles with prompt skeletons)\n  - Animation-specific knowledge base (render pipeline timing, CSS\n    transition vs animation subsystem independence, jsdom test boundaries,\n    React key reuse mechanism)\n  - Confidence calibration template (4-dimension scoring before commit)\n  - Anti-patterns catalog (9 specific traps from this project)\n  - 17-item launch checklist\n\nCase studies reference the actual fix commits in this project. Doc is\nproject-archived at docs/superpowers/methodology/ so it remains discoverable\nfor future contributors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bbf76ddb1e914065abf8a2fd9a0051dc1a54b11c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/git/trees/bbf76ddb1e914065abf8a2fd9a0051dc1a54b11c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/git/commits/a0cb1541301a040396ed23e1bbb8985d1ce59417","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3529490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis","id":3529490,"login":"Caldis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Mjk0OTA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis/react-zmage/commit/a0cb1541301a040396ed23e1bbb8985d1ce59417","node_id":"C_kwDOBnXMktoAKGEwY2IxNTQxMzAxYTA0MDM5NmVkMjNlMWJiYjg5ODVkMWNlNTk0MTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis/react-zmage/commit/2fda167e34bae53e9f6c7b2fbcc7b22dd6b4d9b5","sha":"2fda167e34bae53e9f6c7b2fbcc7b22dd6b4d9b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/commits/2fda167e34bae53e9f6c7b2fbcc7b22dd6b4d9b5"}],"sha":"a0cb1541301a040396ed23e1bbb8985d1ce59417","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/commits/a0cb1541301a040396ed23e1bbb8985d1ce59417"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3529490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis","id":3529490,"login":"Caldis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Mjk0OTA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/commits/2fda167e34bae53e9f6c7b2fbcc7b22dd6b4d9b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-29T18:25:00Z","email":"mail@caldis.me","name":"Caldis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-29T18:25:00Z","email":"mail@caldis.me","name":"Caldis"},"message":"fix(core): pagination shortest-path + jump fade fallback (Issue 1 / Issue 2)\n\nTwo related bugs both stem from `pageWithStep` advancing by raw step in\nhandleSwitchPages, which controls React key alignment for pre-fetch ring reuse:\n\n  Issue 2: N=6 + loop=true on page 0:\n    - Left arrow → image 6: step=-1, pageWithStep+=-1, new center key matches\n      old step-1 (image 6) → React reuse → slide-in animation.\n    - Pagination dot 6 → image 6: handleToPage uses raw `targetPage - page = +5`.\n      pageWithStep+=+5, no key match anywhere → fresh mount → no animation.\n    User expects both paths to animate (image 6 is in pre-fetch ring at step-1).\n\n  Issue 1 (user directive): for any flip mode except ''none'', page changes\n    exceeding the ±2 pre-fetch range should be downgraded to fade transition\n    instead of (a) sweeping intermediate images via wrong-direction key reuse\n    or (b) silently fresh-mounting with no animation.\n\nThree coordinated fixes:\n\n1. utils/resolveShortestStep + computeMinPageDistance (new pure helpers)\n   Loop-aware shortest path between two pages. Replaces raw subtraction in\n   handleToPage so dot 0→5 (N=6 loop=true) resolves to step=-1, fixing Issue 2.\n\n2. Browser.handleSwitchPages cap pageWithStep advance\n   When |step|>2, advance pageWithStep by Math.sign(step) instead of full step.\n   This breaks all React key alignment between old and new render → all imgs\n   fresh-mount, eliminating the wrong-direction sweep (the trade we accepted\n   in the prior wave''s \"图 2、3 sweep\" discussion) and giving Image cdU a\n   clean center node to apply fade-in to.\n\n   Math.sign cap is sufficient because new center src=set[newPage] cannot\n   collide with the only old key at imageIndexWithStep=X+sign(step) (which\n   has src=set[(oldPage+sign(step))%N], distinct from set[newPage] since\n   |originalStep|>2). Verified by hand-tracing N=4/6/10 cases.\n\n3. Image.tsx jumpFadeIn class via CSS @keyframes\n   cdU autonomously detects \"is this a jump?\" by computing minPageDistance\n   between prevProps.page and currProps.page (loop-aware). When >2 AND flip\n   mode != ''none'' AND show, applies CSS class triggering opacity 0→1 keyframe.\n   setTimeout removes class after animationDuration+10ms.\n\n   Why CSS @keyframes (not transition or WAAPI):\n   - Independent of CSS transition subsystem → setNodeTransitionNone (used\n     by scale calibration interrupt landed in commit 0664d82) does NOT\n     interrupt running animations. The two fixes coexist cleanly without\n     visible blip.\n   - jsdom WAAPI stub is incomplete; classList check is deterministic.\n\n   Why Math.sign cap (not advance=0):\n   - Sign-preserving advance gives new center a unique imageIndexWithStep\n     that doesn''t share even the X position with the old center, avoiding\n     ambiguous src disambiguation.\n\nTests added (14 new, 92→106 total):\n- utils helpers: 9 unit tests for resolveShortestStep and computeMinPageDistance\n  covering N∈{1,2,3,6,8,10}, raw step ranges, loop on/off, equal-distance\n  tie-break.\n- Issue 2 lock: N=6 loop pagination 0→5 verifies new center === old step-1\n  DOM identity (key reuse via React).\n- Issue 1 lock: N=6 pagination 0→3 (out-of-range) verifies center.className\n  contains ''jumpFadeIn'' synchronously after click + class removed after\n  360ms timer.\n- flip=''none'' exception: same scenario, verifies no jumpFadeIn class.\n- In-range preserved: N=6 pagination 0→2 (|step|=2) verifies key reuse\n  still works AND no jumpFadeIn class.\n- StrictMode cleanup: unmount mid-fade verifies timer is cancelled.\n\nVerification:\n- 106/106 unit + integration tests passing\n- tsup build clean (ESM/CJS/SSR)\n- pnpm -w run check: 4 sandboxes (r17/r18/r19/nextjs) + 3 SSR smoke pass\n- Public API / defaults / CSS keyframes added (additive only); no breaking change\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9e8d20b289387ffd0f6958428d08cc4e8890aa39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/git/trees/9e8d20b289387ffd0f6958428d08cc4e8890aa39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/git/commits/2fda167e34bae53e9f6c7b2fbcc7b22dd6b4d9b5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3529490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis","id":3529490,"login":"Caldis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Mjk0OTA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis/react-zmage/commit/2fda167e34bae53e9f6c7b2fbcc7b22dd6b4d9b5","node_id":"C_kwDOBnXMktoAKDJmZGExNjdlMzRiYWU1M2U5ZjZjN2IyZmJjYzdiMjJkZDZiNGQ5YjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis/react-zmage/commit/0664d8226fcc598c18697f34a4401c840dfd450c","sha":"0664d8226fcc598c18697f34a4401c840dfd450c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/commits/0664d8226fcc598c18697f34a4401c840dfd450c"}],"sha":"2fda167e34bae53e9f6c7b2fbcc7b22dd6b4d9b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/commits/2fda167e34bae53e9f6c7b2fbcc7b22dd6b4d9b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3529490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Caldis","id":3529490,"login":"Caldis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Mjk0OTA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caldis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/commits/0664d8226fcc598c18697f34a4401c840dfd450c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-29T17:26:36Z","email":"mail@caldis.me","name":"Caldis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-29T17:26:36Z","email":"mail@caldis.me","name":"Caldis"},"message":"fix(core): cancel scale-calibration transition when dim arrives after page change\n\nTwo related bugs both stem from imageDimensions[page] being absent on first\nrender of a fresh-mounted center node — getStyle falls back to currentStyle.scale\n(= previous page''s fit), then onLoad records dims, React re-renders with the\ncorrect ownFitScale, and the CSS transition rule animates 350ms between the two:\n\n  Bug 1: flip=''none'' has no side preloading → every first switch shows the\n  scale animation when adjacent images differ in aspect ratio.\n\n  Bug 2: flip=''swipe'' pagination jumps outside the ±2 pre-render ring (e.g.\n  page 0→3 with N=6, where {1,2,4,5} are pre-rendered via loop wrap but page 3\n  is not) — same race manifests visibly under swipe because opacity stays at\n  1 throughout (other modes mask the scale jump behind opacity 0→1).\n\nFix: a single `pendingDimCalibration: number | null` instance flag set on\npage change when the target page''s dims are absent. When dims later arrive\nvia onLoad → handleRecordImageDimensions, cdU detects the absent→present\ntransition for that exact page and imperatively calls setNodeTransitionNone\non the center img — cancelling the queued CSS transition before the browser\npaints — then restores inline transition via RAF.\n\nWhy pendingDimCalibration over a simpler `currentStyle._type === ''browsing''`\nguard: the latter has a hole — when onLoad lands during the cover→browsing\nanimation (50–400ms after open), _type is already ''browsing'' and the interrupt\nwould freeze the legitimate cover→browsing animation mid-flight. The flag is\nonly set when a page change actually occurred, so initial open''s first dim\narrival is naturally exempt.\n\nWhy this doesn''t break legitimate flip transitions (the trap that an earlier\nsession''s blanket \"transition: none on page change\" approach hit): in-ring\npage changes reuse the side image''s DOM node as the new center via React key\nmatching; that node''s dims were recorded by its earlier sideOnLoad, so the\nflag stays null and the interrupt never fires — leaving opacity 0→1 / slide\nanimations to play through CSS transitions on the reused node as intended.\n\nDefenses layered into the interrupt:\n  - debounceUpdateCurrentImageStyle.cancel() prevents a delayed setCurrentStyle\n    from re-triggering the same transition 50ms later.\n  - Closure capture of imageRef node in the RAF callback restores transition\n    on the original node, even if rapid page changes shifted imageRef.current\n    to a fresh mount.\n  - props.show guard skips interrupt during close path, where closing-follow\n    RAF imperatively manages transform.\n  - cWU cancels calibrationRestoreRaf alongside other RAF handles, matching\n    the project''s \"all cleanup must be cancelable\" invariant.\n\nTests:\n  - flip=''none'' AR-changing page change → inline transition becomes ''none''\n    after onLoad, transform snaps to ownFit, restores '''' after RAF (Bug 1).\n  - flip=''swipe'' pagination 0→3 (N=6 mixed AR) same lock (Bug 2).\n  - flip=''crossFade'' in-ring step+1 with pre-loaded dims → interrupt does\n    NOT fire (legitimate flip transition preserved).\n  - cover→browsing animation with delayed onLoad (>50ms) does NOT trigger\n    interrupt (validates pendingDimCalibration > _type guard).\n  - getImageTransition(''none'', ''browsing'', ''idle'') falls through to\n    touchTransition (locks against ''add none to flip===false guard'' regression\n    that would break rotate/zoom-toggle/resize animations).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4a3791608345dbb97faa5170e8b19cacdc972fa5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/git/trees/4a3791608345dbb97faa5170e8b19cacdc972fa5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Caldis/react-zmage/git/commits/0664d8226fcc598c18697f34a4401c840dfd450c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https