llowers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mlwill07","id":23111872,"login":"mlwill07","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMTExODcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CanopyTax/eslint-config-canopy/commits/d1839cc43a11536ebb3f361972953007f2c511c9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T16:02:45Z","email":"mlwill07@gmail.com","name":"Miriam"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T16:08:07Z","email":"mlwill07@gmail.com","name":"Miriam"},"message":"fix: address review on comment-length\n\n- Exempt inline JSDoc: `/**@type {Foo}*/` puts the tag straight against\n  `/**`, so the `@` is preceded by `*` rather than whitespace and the\n  block was measured instead of exempted. Allow `*` before the tag.\n- Restore the require-subscribe-cleanup rationale, which the shortening\n  pass mangled into \"cannot be one and hid leaks\" and dropped the\n  `return` from its example.\n- Fix the docs'' incorrect-code examples, which were all under the 240\n  limit and so demonstrated the opposite of what they claimed. One also\n  closed its own block comment early on a literal `*/`, and another\n  carried a real @tag that would have exempted it.\n- Document the per-repo `max` override, so a repo wanting a tighter cap\n  does not have to work it out from the flat-config replace semantics.\n- Add tests for inline tags, a tagless inline block, and a mid-word `@`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"293b9e48829f945bf240f07d28b74ea45c52e476","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CanopyTax/eslint-config-canopy/git/trees/293b9e48829f945bf240f07d28b74ea45c52e476"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CanopyTax/eslint-config-canopy/git/commits/d1839cc43a11536ebb3f361972953007f2c511c9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23111872?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mlwill07","id":23111872,"login":"mlwill07","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMTExODcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/CanopyTax/eslint-config-canopy/commit/d1839cc43a11536ebb3f361972953007f2c511c9","node_id":"C_kwDOBqbUlNoAKGQxODM5Y2M0M2ExMTUzNmViYjNmMzYxOTcyOTUzMDA3ZjJjNTExYzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/CanopyTax/eslint-config-canopy/commit/ff49f072309fa5b59c24452a007f87802b0f61ac","sha":"ff49f072309fa5b59c24452a007f87802b0f61ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CanopyTax/eslint-config-canopy/commits/ff49f072309fa5b59c24452a007f87802b0f61ac"}],"sha":"d1839cc43a11536ebb3f361972953007f2c511c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CanopyTax/eslint-config-canopy/commits/d1839cc43a11536ebb3f361972953007f2c511c9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23111872?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mlwill07","id":23111872,"login":"mlwill07","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMTExODcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CanopyTax/eslint-config-canopy/commits/ff49f072309fa5b59c24452a007f87802b0f61ac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T19:05:39Z","email":"mlwill07@gmail.com","name":"Miriam"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T16:07:52Z","email":"mlwill07@gmail.com","name":"Miriam"},"message":"feat: add canopy/comment-length rule (v5.4.0)\n\nAdd a rule that caps a comment at a configurable length (default 240\ncharacters, ~2-3 lines). Consecutive // lines are measured as one\nparagraph so stacking // does not evade the limit; each block comment is\nmeasured whole. Exempt are structured JSDoc blocks (a /** */ carrying an\n@tag) and comments containing a URL; tagless doc blocks and directives\nare not, so a genuinely long comment needs an explicit eslint-disable.\n\nShips at ''error'' — unlike the other canopy rules at ''warn'' — so adopting\n5.4.0 will surface build-breaking errors on existing long comments.\nConsumers can soften per-repo with [''warn'', { max }]. A minor bump, not a\npatch, so a consumer on a caret range opts into that deliberately rather\nthan picking up a build-breaking rule on a routine update.\n\nAlso shortens this repo''s own over-length rationale comments so it lints\nclean against the new rule.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7b5187de1d2737d3f0753a3cb8d2511e19ad2976","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CanopyTax/eslint-config-canopy/git/trees/7b5187de1d2737d3f0753a3cb8d2511e19ad2976"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CanopyTax/eslint-config-canopy/git/commits/ff49f072309fa5b59c24452a007f87802b0f61ac","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23111872?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mlwill07","id":23111872,"login":"mlwill07","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMTExODcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlwill07","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/CanopyTax/eslint-config-canopy/commit/ff49f072309fa5b59c24452a007f87802b0f61ac","node_id":"C_kwDOBqbUlNoAKGZmNDlmMDcyMzA5ZmE1YjU5YzI0NDUyYTAwN2Y4NzgwMmIwZjYxYWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/CanopyTa