":"https://api.github.com/users/rhys-childs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhys-childs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhys-childs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CanopyTax/eslint-config-canopy/commits/ec2a14b3ec7dda7b067515ec0c52874646bb6846/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:52:42Z","email":"rhys.childs@canopytax.com","name":"rhys-childs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:52:42Z","email":"rhys.childs@canopytax.com","name":"rhys-childs"},"message":"fix: point no-window-auth-globals at the named exports for non-React code\n\nThe rule message and docs offered no replacement usable outside a React\ntree, which is exactly where the rule fires most (root-config activity\nfunctions, bootstraps). mobile-root-config resolved the warning with\nAuth.getLoggedInUser()?.role off the default import — undefined at\nruntime, broke the mobile client-portal — because the only non-hook\nguidance was \"observables or eslint-disable\".\n\n- Rule message now names getLoggedInUser()/getTenant() and says they are\n  named exports, not on the default auth object.\n- Docs gain a non-React example and the default-vs-named warning, and the\n  \"When Not To Use It\" section now recommends the named exports instead\n  of leaving a gap.\n- Fixes the correct-code example destructuring useWithUserAndTenant() as\n  an object; it returns a [user, tenant] tuple.\n\nBumps to 5.3.1 so the merge publishes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c591de55ea43cd2c65f953e2fbdfd3cba22ee3a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CanopyTax/eslint-config-canopy/git/trees/c591de55ea43cd2c65f953e2fbdfd3cba22ee3a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CanopyTax/eslint-config-canopy/git/commits/ec2a14b3ec7dda7b067515ec0c52874646bb6846","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_a