f3b946099dc80c93005b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrisjwalk/angular-cli-netcore-ngrx-starter/commits/b79ca281f12583f3804f3b946099dc80c93005b4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268224883?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/chrisjwalk-bot","id":268224883,"login":"chrisjwalk-bot","node_id":"U_kgDOD_zJcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrisjwalk/angular-cli-netcore-ngrx-starter/commits/8e2ef26d80a9c8e3fef63c960877cc78e43b9883/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-08T00:02:02Z","email":"268224883+chrisjwalk-bot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"chrisjwalk-bot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-08T00:02:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: upgrade to Angular 22 with peer dep overrides (closes #174) (#175)\n\n* feat: upgrade to Angular 22 with peer dep overrides (closes #174)\n\n- Bumped all @angular/* to 22.0.0, @angular-devkit/* to 22.0.0\n- Bumped @angular-eslint/* and angular-eslint to 22.0.0\n- Bumped @analogjs/* to 2.6.0, @testing-library/angular to 19.4.1\n- Bumped @module-federation/vite to 1.16.4\n- Updated all other outdated packages (vite, vitest, marked, etc.)\n- Added peerDependencyRules.allowedVersions for Angular 22\n  to satisfy Nx and NgRx peer dep caps\n- Build, all 11 test suites, all 31 E2E tests pass\n- MFE integration test passes with zero JS errors\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore: bump GitHub Actions versions\n\n- pnpm/action-setup v4 → v6 (all workflows)\n- marocchino/sticky-pull-request-comment v2 → v3 (ci.yml)\n- azure/login v2 → v3 (deploy.yml)\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: move robots.txt and favicon.ico to public/ for Vite static serving\n\nVite only copies static assets from the public/ directory into\nthe build output. Both robots.txt and favicon.ico were in src/\nwhich meant the SPA fallback returned index.html for /robots.txt.\nLighthouse flagged 63 robots.txt validation errors (HTML response).\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* test: add PWA update notification E2E tests and fix host display\n\n- Add data-testid to NotificationList and NotificationBell components\n- Add class: ''block'' to MainToolbar host for correct display\n- Add pwa-update.e2e.spec.ts with 4 tests:\n  - Bell visibility in toolbar\n  - Bell click opens notification overlay with empty state\n  - SW registration (CI-only, skipped in dev)\n  - Full SW update notification flow with route interception (CI-only)\n- All 33 E2E tests pass (2 skipped), all 11 unit test suites pass\n\n* ci: add E2E tests to CI workflow running against production build\n\n- Added E2E test execution steps to CI workflow (Playwright browser install, E2E run, report upload)\n- Playwright webServer uses production builds in CI (serve-e2e:production, serve:production)\n- This ensures PWA service worker is enabled and SW update notification tests work\n- Test results upload includes both Playwright artifacts and JUnit reports\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: remove unsupported --configuration flag from e2e:ci\n\nPlaywright CLI does not support --configuration. The playwright.config.ts\nalready uses process.env.CI to switch between dev and production builds.\nSetting CI=true is sufficient to trigger production builds in CI.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: install Firefox alongside Chromium for E2E tests\n\nPlaywright config has both chromium and firefox projects. Only chromium\nwas installed, causing all 37 Firefox tests to fail with ''Executable\ndoesn''t exist''. All 31 Chromium tests pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: use CI env var for PWA SW test skip condition\n\nbuilds with PWA enabled, so SW tests run there but skip in local dev.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: increase timeout for cold-cache content E2E tests in CI\n\nThe content.e2e.spec.ts runs first alphabetically, so the browser has a\ncold cache when navigating to /content. The lazy-loaded chunk download\nexceeds the default 5-second Playwright expect timeout on CI runners.\n\nCloses #174\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: serve real sw.js via route interception for PWA E2E tests\n\nVite dev server returns HTML (SPA fallback) for /sw.js, which prevents\nservice worker registration. Read the actual sw.js from the production\nbuild output and serve it via Playwright route interception.\n\nAlso:\n- Fix serve-static target path (browser → client)\n- Add browser console error capture to content tests for flakiness debugging\n- Fix TS4111 errors in playwright.config.ts (dot → bracket notation)\n\n(closes #174)\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): wait for content.routes chunk before asserting content page\n\nUse Promise.all with page.waitForResponse targeting content.routes-*\nchunk instead of racing page.goto against assertions. The cold-cache\nlazy chunk load can exceed the previous 15s timeout on CI''s first\nrequest to the preview server.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): replace waitForResponse with 60s timeouts for content page tests\n\nThe waitForResponse approach could not match content.routes chunks in\nproduction Vite builds (lazy routes are inlined differently). Reverted to\nsimple page.goto with generous 60s timeouts for cold-cache CI runs.\n\nAlso converted SW_JS from an IIFE to a function in PWA E2E tests to\navoid reading the file at module import time.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"dcd937779f63202c3620155f00684c3b7954a8c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrisjwalk/angular-cli-netcore-ngrx-starter/git/trees/dcd937779f63202c3620155f00684c3b7954a8c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrisjwalk/angular-cli-netcore-ngrx-starter/git/commits/8e2ef26d80a9c8e3fef63c960877cc78e43b9883","verification":{"payload":"tree dcd937779f63202c3620155f00684c3b7954a8c9\nparent 7630c8d32a79f03bbabc80df7aab7bddbb85fd09\nauthor chrisjwalk-bot <268224883+chrisjwalk-bot@users.noreply.github.com> 1780876922 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780876922 -0400\n\nfeat: upgrade to Angular 22 with peer dep overrides (closes #174) (#175)\n\n* feat: upgrade to Angular 22 with peer dep overrides (closes #174)\n\n- Bumped all @angular/* to 22.0.0, @angular-devkit/* to 22.0.0\n- Bumped @angular-eslint/* and angular-eslint to 22.0.0\n- Bumped @analogjs/* to 2.6.0, @testing-library/angular to 19.4.1\n- Bumped @module-federation/vite to 1.16.4\n- Updated all other outdated packages (vite, vitest, marked, etc.)\n- Added peerDependencyRules.allowedVersions for Angular 22\n  to satisfy Nx and NgRx peer dep caps\n- Build, all 11 test suites, all 31 E2E tests pass\n- MFE integration test passes with zero JS errors\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore: bump GitHub Actions versions\n\n- pnpm/action-setup v4 → v6 (all workflows)\n- marocchino/sticky-pull-request-comment v2 → v3 (ci.yml)\n- azure/login v2 → v3 (deploy.yml)\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: move robots.txt and favicon.ico to public/ for Vite static serving\n\nVite only copies static assets from the public/ directory into\nthe build output. Both robots.txt and favicon.ico were in src/\nwhich meant the SPA fallback returned index.html for /robots.txt.\nLighthouse flagged 63 robots.txt validation errors (HTML response).\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* test: add PWA update notification E2E tests and fix host display\n\n- Add data-testid to NotificationList and NotificationBell components\n- Add class: ''block'' to MainToolbar host for correct display\n- Add pwa-update.e2e.spec.ts with 4 tests:\n  - Bell visibility in toolbar\n  - Bell click opens notification overlay with empty state\n  - SW registration (CI-only, skipped in dev)\n  - Full SW update notification flow with route interception (CI-only)\n- All 33 E2E tests pass (2 skipped), all 11 unit test suites pass\n\n* ci: add E2E tests to CI workflow running against production build\n\n- Added E2E test execution steps to CI workflow (Playwright browser install, E2E run, report upload)\n- Playwright webServer uses production builds in CI (serve-e2e:production, serve:production)\n- This ensures PWA service worker is enabled and SW update notification tests work\n- Test results upload includes both Playwright artifacts and JUnit reports\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: remove unsupported --configuration flag from e2e:ci\n\nPlaywright CLI does not support --configuration. The playwright.config.ts\nalready uses process.env.CI to switch between dev and production builds.\nSetting CI=true is sufficient to trigger production builds in CI.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: install Firefox alongside Chromium for E2E tests\n\nPlaywright config has both chromium and firefox projects. Only chromium\nwas installed, causing all 37 Firefox tests to fail with ''Executable\ndoesn''t exist''. All 31 Chromium tests pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: use CI env var for PWA SW test skip condition\n\nbuilds with PWA enabled, so SW tests run there but skip in local dev.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: increase timeout for cold-cache content E2E tests in CI\n\nThe content.e2e.spec.ts runs first alphabetically, so the browser has a\ncold cache when navigating to /content. The lazy-loaded chunk download\nexceeds the default 5-second Playwright expect timeout on CI runners.\n\nCloses #174\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: serve real sw.js via route interception for PWA E2E tests\n\nVite dev server returns HTML (SPA fallback) for /sw.js, which prevents\nservice worker registration. Read the actual sw.js from the production\nbuild output and serve it via Playwright route interception.\n\nAlso:\n- Fix serve-static target path (browser → client)\n- Add browser console error capture to content tests for flakiness debugging\n- Fix TS4111 errors in playwright.config.ts (dot → bracket notation)\n\n(closes #174)\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): wait for content.routes chunk before asserting content page\n\nUse Promise.all with page.waitForResponse targeting content.routes-*\nchunk instead of racing page.goto against assertions. The cold-cache\nlazy chunk load can exceed the previous 15s timeout on CI''s first\nrequest to the preview server.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): replace waitForResponse with 60s timeouts for content page tests\n\nThe waitForResponse approach could not match content.routes chunks in\nproduction Vite builds (lazy routes are inlined differently). Reverted to\nsimple page.goto with generous 60s timeouts for cold-cache CI runs.\n\nAlso converted SW_JS from an IIFE to a function in PWA E2E tests to\navoid reading the file at module import time.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJgZ6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdNwQAH9K6VE6n7iLnxCjrItpOgjg\n+IpB2jRSwA8jthzhNh3fE8QVvvicRuQeQluFLHA/nvOMOzPw/1gP5vhG1nrZibBN\n82YKQe3/GPP+Ap04abqv1bz9VERdzNyWJjDO/vkmRWSOaJxFoijzYJFBBoOPky25\nefx9O8SMkkunAOh3V7eSLQ2PihL9I7fVAa49nk+tQ0VirrzziL6cnn/QUIrBW+NK\nXbQnnA2BpAcK20ie7Cxya24+bx90+fV6cGJUE0v+vKVgtZYcNkKz5MqpeEYlpmYt\n+ilCcciRW9mknZLDYF87AQiehhXZhHSdy77Kg1+P9AvY1ua+jEMXJih19rv0ECnp\nN5pzuNHnhSZzOSg995ERtnr5vR2aFrloVHVIOwr1bZM+76/7GOGcvqhnRNgqTsPK\nVyASVILBx09PaHyvbAG5kdv4N3/HHpqg+XMCT8tMB4VhiV2r3lo9gJUkdszsebo8\n+lCXjkw72qYVRQ/zmbxixGYgEaTDM9CFsLBLykaNboDfbTbo0Rsd76hfoBIxcoAZ\nQOv08LHAUu6Xfg8q4zMYcRhqjhanYDoo258LZQWv/q/UxXN57st8nzOJWEZmebKJ\nk//9S+1AcD5UYG/Nq+RxDrPKCIBgTkLKmb27dPt+EY01aNzKymgP2/M+WZsCbQJk\naUJ3yMs+gClcZAGJLvqh\n=4SRS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-08T00:02:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/chrisjwalk/angular-cli-netcore-ngrx-starter/commit/8e2ef26d80a9c8e3fef63c960877cc78e43b9883","node_id":"C_kwDOBucjadoAKDhlMmVmMjZkODBhOWM4ZTNmZWY2M2M5NjA4NzdjYzc4ZTQzYjk4ODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/chrisjwalk/angular-cli-netcore-ngrx-starter/commit/7630c8d32a79f03bbabc80df7aab7bddbb85fd09","sha":"7630c8d32a79f03bbabc80df7aab7bddbb85fd09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrisjwalk/angular-cli-netcore-ngrx-starter/commits/7630c8d32a79f03bbabc80df7aab7bddbb85fd09"}],"sha":"8e2ef26d80a9c8e3fef63c960877cc78e43b9883","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrisjwalk/angular-cli-netcore-ngrx-starter/commits/8e2ef26d80a9c8e3fef63c960877cc78e43b9883"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268224883?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/chrisjwalk-bot","id":268224883,"login":"chrisjwalk-bot","node_id":"U_kgDOD_zJcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrisjwalk/angular-cli-netcore-ngrx-starter/commits/7630c8d32a79f03bbabc80df7aab7bddbb85fd09/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T19:14:21Z","email":"268224883+chrisjwalk-bot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"chrisjwalk-bot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T19:14:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add micro-frontend example using @module-federation/vite (#169)\n\n* feat: add micro-frontend example using @module-federation/vite (closes #168)\n\n- Add apps/counter-remote as MFE remote (port 4201, exposes ./Routes)\n- Configure @module-federation/vite 1.16.2 on both host and remote\n- Use federation() plugin disabled in test mode to avoid Vitest conflicts\n- Add mfe-counter route to web-app using dynamic import(''counter-remote/Routes'')\n- Add MFE Counter nav link in shared nav-links\n- Add TypeScript module declaration for counter-remote/Routes\n- Externalize virtual:pwa-register in remote build (tree-shaken, not instantiated)\n- Set chrome89 build target on both host and remote for top-level await support\n- Add passWithNoTests + tsconfig.spec.json to counter-remote for empty test suite\n- Known limitation: LayoutStore singleton — remote bundles its own copy of\n  @myorg/shared, so nav title won''t update when loaded as MFE (workspace libs\n  cannot be in MF shared config, only npm packages)\n- Demo targets nx serve (dev mode); @module-federation/vite issue #707 (async\n  __loadShare__ wrappers) may affect production builds with ng-content components\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: normalize server.watch for @module-federation/vite Vite 8 compatibility\n\n@module-federation/vite crashes when server.watch is boolean false.\nThe @nx/vite build executor defaults watch to false, which gets merged\ninto the inline config before plugin config hooks run. A pre-enforce\nplugin ensures server.watch is an object before the federation hook sees it.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: auto-start counter-remote when serving web-app\n\n- Add counter-remote:serve to web-app serve dependsOn\n- Add continuous: true to counter-remote serve target\n- Add normalize-server-watch plugin to counter-remote vite config\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(counter-remote): stub virtual:pwa-register for dev server\n\nThe host provides virtual:pwa-register via vite-plugin-pwa, but the\nremote''s dev server pre-transforms shared libs independently and can''t\nresolve it. A no-op virtual plugin stubs it out so the dev server\nstarts cleanly.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: share @ngrx/signals as singleton in MFE config to resolve NG0200\n\nBoth host and remote were bundling separate copies of @ngrx/signals,\ncreating duplicate DI token identities for platform-scoped services\n(Dispatcher, Events, ReducerEvents). Angular''s DI detected this as\na circular dependency (NG0200) when the SignalStore-based CounterStore\nwas instantiated via the MFE route.\n\nSharing @ngrx/signals and @ngrx/signals/events as singletons ensures\na single set of class tokens across the federation boundary, fixing\nthe circular dependency error on navigation to /mfe-counter.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(mfe): share Angular CDK, Material, and workspace libs as singletons\n\nPrevents NG0912 component ID collision warnings by ensuring all Angular\nCDK and Material sub-path packages, plus workspace libs (@myorg/counter,\n@myorg/shared), are shared as singletons in both host and remote vite\nconfigs. Previously only core Angular packages were shared, causing\nCDK/Material components and workspace-lib components to be bundled\nseparately in each app and registered twice with Angular''s component ID\nregistry.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(mfe): remove workspace libs from shared (MF virtual module limitation)\n\nMF virtual modules can''t enumerate export * chains from TypeScript path\naliases, causing [MISSING_EXPORT] build errors. Workspace libs must\nremain as separate bundles in each app.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(mfe): add missing material/divider and material/sidenav to MF shared singletons\n\nBoth @angular/material/divider and @angular/material/sidenav are\nimported by workspace libs (@myorg/shared) which are loaded by both\nthe host and remote. Adding them as singletons prevents NG0912\ncomponent ID collisions for MatDivider, MatSidenav, etc.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: mfe example with counter remote (closes #168)\n\n- add counter-remote app exposing counter lib via module federation\n- fix NG0912 collisions: import:false on CDK/Material in remote sharedDeps\n- fix test OXC failures: fastCompile:mode===''test'' in host analog() call\n  (angular files outside tsconfig.spec.json compiled by fast-compile AOT;\n   non-Angular TS stripped by OXC lang:''ts'' instead of lang:''js'')\n- remove /feature duplicate route; /mfe-counter is the single MFE entry\n- update README with MFE architecture section\n- add .claude/skills/create-mfe SKILL.md documenting the full setup\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: use single wildcard in SWA navigationFallback exclude paths\n\nAzure Static Web Apps allows at most one ''*'' per route pattern.\nReplace ''/counter-remote/**'' with two single-wildcard patterns.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore: update GitHub Actions to Node.js 24 compatible versions\n\nBump actions/checkout and actions/setup-node from v4 to v6 in\npreview.yml and deploy.yml to avoid Node.js 20 deprecation warnings.\nAlso align actions/setup-dotnet to v5 in deploy.yml.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: resolve CounterContainer stub and update E2E tests for /mfe-counter\n\n- counter-remote-routes.ts: re-export counterRoutes directly from\n  @myorg/counter instead of importing CounterContainer (which is not\n  in the lib''s barrel export), fixing NG04014 in CI integration tests\n- E2E tests: update URL assertions from /feature to /mfe-counter\n- playwright.config.ts: add counter-remote:serve webServer so MFE\n  remote is available during E2E runs\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: build counter-remote before copying into web-app output in CI\n\nIn preview.yml the copy step ran before web-app build, so the build\nwipe wiped the counter-remote files. Fix: build both apps first, then\ncopy counter-remote into web-app/client/counter-remote/.\n\nIn deploy.yml counter-remote was never built or deployed at all. Add\nbuild + copy steps and set COUNTER_REMOTE_ENTRY=/counter-remote/remoteEntry.js\nso the host resolves the MFE correctly in production.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs: update create-mfe skill with accurate patterns and pitfalls\n\n- Fix step order: generate lib first, then remote app\n- Add required barrel export and remotes.d.ts type declaration steps\n- Clarify remote app shell files must be kept (keep main.ts, app.config.ts etc)\n- Fix @module-federation/vite placement: devDependencies not dependencies\n- Add checklist of vite.config.ts fields to update when cloning counter-remote\n- Fix test stub: prefer re-exporting lib routes over importing components\n  directly (avoids NG04014 when component is not in barrel)\n- Fix CI build order: copy after BOTH builds, not before host build\n  (host build wipes its output dir, destroying the copied remote files)\n- Fix SWA wildcards: use /* not /** (SWA only allows one * per segment)\n- Add E2E section with playwright webServer entries\n- Add missing pitfalls: NG04014, remote files wiped by host build\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: persist counter state across navigation by providing store at root level\n\nMove CounterStore from component-scoped providers to providedIn: ''root''\nso the state survives when navigating away from and back to the counter route.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: move PWA icons to Vite publicDir so they are included in the build output\n\nIcons in src/assets/icons/ were not being copied to dist because Vite''s\npublicDir defaults to <root>/public, not src/. Moving them to\npublic/assets/icons/ ensures they are served at /assets/icons/*.png\nin the deployed app, fixing 404s for PWA manifest icons in SWA.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: remove deprecated provideAnimations to fix MFE loadShare bug (fixes #168)\n\nprovideAnimations() from @angular/platform-browser/animations resolves to\nundefined through the @module-federation/vite loadShare mechanism, causing\n\"TypeError: Ut is not a function\" in the deployed preview.\n\nSince provideAnimations() is deprecated in Angular 21+ (animations are now\nprovided automatically by the platform), removing the explicit call eliminates\nthe broken loadShare dependency.\n\nAlso added an MFE integration e2e test that guards against JS load errors.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore: update pnpm allowBuilds\n\n* fix: remove @ngrx/signals/events to fix MFE NG0203 error (closes #168)\n\n- Removed injectDispatch, eventGroup, on, withReducer from CounterStore\n- Consolidated into single signalStore with withMethods + patchState\n- Removed @ngrx/signals/events and @angular/animations from counter-remote shared deps\n- The root cause: @module-federation/vite generates same loadShare path for\n  @ngrx/signals and @ngrx/signals/events, inlining a separate copy of\n  @angular/core internals (_injectImplementation) that is never set during\n  host DI, causing takeUntilDestroyed() to fail with NG0203.\n- Updated counter E2E tests: all 31 passed (including MFE integration)\n- Local verification: counter MFE renders with zero JS errors\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: restore @ngrx/signals requiredVersion to ~21.1.0 (matches installed)\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: restore @ngrx/signals requiredVersion to ~21.1.0 in counter-remote too\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: migrate pnpm overrides to workspace yaml, bump CI to pnpm 11\n\n- Moved pnpm.overrides from package.json to pnpm-workspace.yaml (fixes\n  pnpm 11 deprecation warning & CI lockfile mismatch with --frozen-lockfile)\n- Updated all 3 CI workflows to pnpm 11 to match local version\n- Regenerated lockfile\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f35879f96c7ff0f8aa43d8e76cd00ff51432ed8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrisjwalk/angular-cli-netcore-ngrx-starter/git/trees/f35879f96c7ff0f8aa43d8e76cd00ff51432ed8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrisjwalk/angular-cli-netcore-ngrx-starter/git/commits/7630c8d32a79f03bbabc80df7aab7bddbb85fd09","verification":{"payload":"tree f35879f96c7ff0f8aa43d8e76cd00ff51432ed8f\nparent dd7e3260b62f0d46c8df9b0559dc03c396c6a0ae\nauthor chrisjwalk-bot <268224883+chrisjwalk-bot@users.noreply.github.com> 1780859661 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780859661 -0400\n\nfeat: add micro-frontend example using @module-federation/vite (#169)\n\n* feat: add micro-frontend example using @module-federation/vite (closes #168)\n\n- Add apps/counter-remote as MFE remote (port 4201, exposes ./Routes)\n- Configure @module-federation/vite 1.16.2 on both host and remote\n- Use federation() plugin disabled in test mode to avoid Vitest conflicts\n- Add mfe-counter route to web-app using dynamic import(''counter-remote/Routes'')\n- Add MFE Counter nav link in shared nav-links\n- Add TypeScript module declaration for counter-remote/Routes\n- Externalize virtual:pwa-register in remote build (tree-shaken, not instantiated)\n- Set chrome89 build target on both host and remote for top-level await support\n- Add passWithNoTests + tsconfig.spec.json to counter-remote for empty test suite\n- Known limitation: LayoutStore singleton — remote bundles its own copy of\n  @myorg/shared, so nav title won''t update when loaded as MFE (workspace libs\n  cannot be in MF shared config, only npm packages)\n- Demo targets nx serve (dev mode); @module-federation/vite issue #707 (async\n  __loadShare__ wrappers) may affect production builds with ng-content components\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: normalize server.watch for @module-federation/vite Vite 8 compatibility\n\n@module-federation/vite crashes when server.watch is boolean false.\nThe @nx/vite build executor defaults watch to false, which gets merged\ninto the inline config before plugin config hooks run. A pre-enforce\nplugin ensures server.watch is an object before the federation hook sees it.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: auto-start counter-remote when serving web-app\n\n- Add counter-remote:serve to web-app serve dependsOn\n- Add continuous: true to counter-remote serve target\n- Add normalize-server-watch plugin to counter-remote vite config\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(counter-remote): stub virtual:pwa-register for dev server\n\nThe host provides virtual:pwa-register via vite-plugin-pwa, but the\nremote''s dev server pre-transforms shared libs independently and can''t\nresolve it. A no-op virtual plugin stubs it out so the dev server\nstarts cleanly.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: share @ngrx/signals as singleton in MFE config to resolve NG0200\n\nBoth host and remote were bundling separate copies of @ngrx/signals,\ncreating duplicate DI token identities for platform-scoped services\n(Dispatcher, Events, ReducerEvents). Angular''s DI detected this as\na circular dependency (NG0200) when the SignalStore-based CounterStore\nwas instantiated via the MFE route.\n\nSharing @ngrx/signals and @ngrx/signals/events as singletons ensures\na single set of class tokens across the federation boundary, fixing\nthe circular dependency error on navigation to /mfe-counter.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(mfe): share Angular CDK, Material, and workspace libs as singletons\n\nPrevents NG0912 component ID collision warnings by ensuring all Angular\nCDK and Material sub-path packages, plus workspace libs (@myorg/counter,\n@myorg/shared), are shared as singletons in both host and remote vite\nconfigs. Previously only core Angular packages were shared, causing\nCDK/Material components and workspace-lib components to be bundled\nseparately in each app and registered twice with Angular''s component ID\nregistry.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(mfe): remove workspace libs from shared (MF virtual module limitation)\n\nMF virtual modules can''t enumerate export * chains from TypeScript path\naliases, causing [MISSING_EXPORT] build errors. Workspace libs must\nremain as separate bundles in each app.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(mfe): add missing material/divider and material/sidenav to MF shared singletons\n\nBoth @angular/material/divider and @angular/material/sidenav are\nimported by workspace libs (@myorg/shared) which are loaded by both\nthe host and remote. Adding them as singletons prevents NG0912\ncomponent ID collisions for MatDivider, MatSidenav, etc.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: mfe example with counter remote (closes #168)\n\n- add counter-remote app exposing counter lib via module federation\n- fix NG0912 collisions: import:false on CDK/Material in remote sharedDeps\n- fix test OXC failures: fastCompile:mode===''test'' in host analog() call\n  (angular files outside tsconfig.spec.json compiled by fast-compile AOT;\n   non-Angular TS stripped by OXC lang:''ts'' instead of lang:''js'')\n- remove /feature duplicate route; /mfe-counter is the single MFE entry\n- update README with MFE architecture section\n- add .claude/skills/create-mfe SKILL.md documenting the full setup\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: use single wildcard in SWA navigationFallback exclude paths\n\nAzure Static Web Apps allows at most one ''*'' per route pattern.\nReplace ''/counter-remote/**'' with two single-wildcard patterns.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore: update GitHub Actions to Node.js 24 compatible versions\n\nBump actions/checkout and actions/setup-node from v4 to v6 in\npreview.yml and deploy.yml to avoid Node.js 20 deprecation warnings.\nAlso align actions/setup-dotnet to v5 in deploy.yml.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: resolve CounterContainer stub and update E2E tests for /mfe-counter\n\n- counter-remote-routes.ts: re-export counterRoutes directly from\n  @myorg/counter instead of importing CounterContainer (which is not\n  in the lib''s barrel export), fixing NG04014 in CI integration tests\n- E2E tests: update URL assertions from /feature to /mfe-counter\n- playwright.config.ts: add counter-remote:serve webServer so MFE\n  remote is available during E2E runs\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: build counter-remote before copying into web-app output in CI\n\nIn preview.yml the copy step ran before web-app build, so the build\nwipe wiped the counter-remote files. Fix: build both apps first, then\ncopy counter-remote into web-app/client/counter-remote/.\n\nIn deploy.yml counter-remote was never built or deployed at all. Add\nbuild + copy steps and set COUNTER_REMOTE_ENTRY=/counter-remote/remoteEntry.js\nso the host resolves the MFE correctly in production.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs: update create-mfe skill with accurate patterns and pitfalls\n\n- Fix step order: generate lib first, then remote app\n- Add required barrel export and remotes.d.ts type declaration steps\n- Clarify remote app shell files must be kept (keep main.ts, app.config.ts etc)\n- Fix @module-federation/vite placement: devDependencies not dependencies\n- Add checklist of vite.config.ts fields to update when cloning counter-remote\n- Fix test stub: prefer re-exporting lib routes over importing components\n  directly (avoids NG04014 when component is not in barrel)\n- Fix CI build order: copy after BOTH builds, not before host build\n  (host build wipes its output dir, destroying the copied remote files)\n- Fix SWA wildcards: use /* not /** (SWA only allows one * per segment)\n- Add E2E section with playwright webServer entries\n- Add missing pitfalls: NG04014, remote files wiped by host build\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: persist counter state across navigation by providing store at root level\n\nMove CounterStore from component-scoped providers to providedIn: ''root''\nso the state survives when navigating away from and back to the counter route.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: move PWA icons to Vite publicDir so they are included in the build output\n\nIcons in src/assets/icons/ were not being copied to dist because Vite''s\npublicDir defaults to <root>/public, not src/. Moving them to\npublic/assets/icons/ ensures they are served at /assets/icons/*.png\nin the deployed app, fixing 404s for PWA manifest icons in SWA.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: remove deprecated provideAnimations to fix MFE loadShare bug (fixes #168)\n\nprovideAnimations() from @angular/platform-browser/animations resolves to\nundefined through the @module-federation/vite loadShare mechanism, causing\n\"TypeError: Ut is not a function\" in the deployed preview.\n\nSince provideAnimations() is deprecated in Angular 21+ (animations are now\nprovided automatically by the platform), removing the explicit call eliminates\nthe broken loadShare dependency.\n\nAlso added an MFE integration e2e test that guards against JS load errors.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore: update pnpm allowBuilds\n\n* fix: remove @ngrx/signals/events to fix MFE NG0203 error (closes #168)\n\n- Removed injectDispatch, eventGroup, on, withReducer from CounterStore\n- Consolidated into single signalStore with withMethods + patchState\n- Removed @ngrx/signals/events and @angular/animations from counter-remote shared deps\n- The root cause: @module-federation/vite generates same loadShare path for\n  @ngrx/signals and @ngrx/signals/events, inlining a separate copy of\n  @angular/core internals (_injectImplementation) that is never set during\n  host DI, causing takeUntilDestroyed() to fail with NG0203.\n- Updated counter E2E tests: all 31 passed (including MFE integration)\n- Local verification: counter MFE renders with zero JS errors\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: restore @ngrx/signals requiredVersion to ~21.1.0 (matches installed)\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: restore @ngrx/signals requiredVersion to ~21.1.0 in counter-remote too\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: migrate pnpm overrides to workspace yaml, bump CI to pnpm 11\n\n- Moved pnpm.overrides from package.json to pnpm-workspace.yaml (fixes\n  pnpm 11 deprecation warning & CI lockfile mismatch with --frozen-lockfile)\n- Updated all 3 CI workflows to pnpm 11 to match local version\n- Regenerated lockfile\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJcMNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6SsQAGlH9/xiC2BFDB5ERw5DHdY2\nlq+8Uei7rahE109ruZjgoNWN3VBxX7SZVdjw9AUQTN/29g2XJ5tdmOuUjcGuawEU\ncGOI09tQ+rAClbtfrLU4JmtGDnwXZgW7cV5ktn6GsAAiFs6x0EPZFf/kR4KV2oM3\nlD/AH05TUg/DxHF2iF1WPXxJpodW0PurUr6oPE7L4PMHd9Siy2FAys7rwWqizCup\nR8ms8JBey8Rbq6qkHjZDt8WFNJyYuBZhEO2YeC+wwCkTgSwcY6iahglgxpF1PeaB\nive+Uo+YZSfofQAvwKBZ88fDDd+OEpBhgc0zUNtBBMy84+oGu25ufx2iuUjtUXSL\nDdDGwrldcrgq6ODwu99LVXN7GN4FjPti/4gwrLyF/elgJvxn3c0iu7XuIYI9R/nv\nMfyKgTdPBzDmW1ZrE7lDQiGiqb5YxQ696ZzyhyGdJDdWGdUuO+CtK4CZbcqCAsxS\nonEp5vYASGsBWGsE5OuC372stFnNwtE6wEf4XKNzZUJ/oJxT5n8/emwQVYahCzVp\n7f8CsPsydXF8PRPjntb4AjbpOwD8ANx2PJlXSmepm+vB+HZqxsx5DvUFBi/KZRBM\nchoQqA7ExjZZF1bKZAAtalG/AKJKR/pUFBRdKf3P0uTh8opejD1UdjjVtHQlulGV\nKUy5Zxxyl2gCdT8luLHk\n=IuSh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-07T19:14:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/chrisjwalk/angular-cli-netcore-ngrx-starter/commit/7630c8d32a79f03bbabc80df7aab7bddbb85fd09","node_id":"C_kwDOBucjadoAKDc2MzBjOGQzMmE3OWYwM2JiYWJjODBkZjdhYWI3YmRkYmI4NWZkMDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/chrisjwalk/angular-cli-netcore-ngrx-starter/commit/dd7e3260b62f0d46c8df9b0559dc03c396c6a0ae","sha":"dd7e3260b62f0d46c8df9b0559dc03c396c6a0ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrisjwalk/angular-cli-netcore-ngrx-starter/commits/dd7e3260b62f0d46c8df9b0559dc03c396c6a0ae"}],"sha":"7630c8d32a79f03bbabc80df7aab7bddbb85fd09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrisjwalk/angular-cli-netcore-ngrx-starter/commits/7630c8d32a79f03bbabc80df7aab7bddbb85fd09"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268224883?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/chrisjwalk-bot","id":268224883,"login":"chrisjwalk-bot","node_id":"U_kgDOD_zJcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrisjwalk/angular-cli-netcore-ngrx-starter/commits/dd7e3260b62f0d46c8df9b0559dc03c396c6a0ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T16:33:36Z","email":"268224883+chrisjwalk-bot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"chrisjwalk-bot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T16:33:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: address dependabot security alerts (closes #166) (#167)\n\nUpdate pnpm.overrides to force patched versions of transitive deps:\n- qs >= 6.15.2 (DoS via null entries, was >=6.14.2)\n- ws >= 8.20.1 (uninitialized memory disclosure, new)\n- brace-expansion@5 >= 5.0.6 (numeric range DoS, was >=5.0.5)\n- webpack-dev-server >= 5.2.4 (cross-origin source code exposure, new)\n- uuid@8 >= 12.0.1 (buffer bounds check in v3/v5/v6, new)\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"bf2232987459cebe2d8fde47e9d22a1502f78d28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrisjwalk/angular-cli-netcore-ngrx-starter/git/trees/bf2232987459cebe2d8fde47e9d22a1502f78d28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrisjwalk/angular-cli-netcore-ngrx-starter/git/commits/dd7e3260b62f0d46c8df9b0559dc03c396c6a0ae","verification":{"payload":"tree bf2232987459cebe2d8fde47e9d22a1502f78d28\nparent 60b1080e4ad40115671c5bb204b13f5e1d6feb6d\nauthor chrisjwalk-bot <268224883+chrisjwalk-bot@users.noreply.github.com> 1780158816 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780158816 -0400\n\nfix: address dependabot security alerts (closes #166) (#167)\n\nUpdate pnpm.overrides to force patched versions of transitive deps:\n- qs >= 6.15.2 (DoS via null entries, was >=6.14.2)\n- ws >= 8.20.1 (uninitialized memory disclosure, new)\n- brace-expansion@5 >= 5.0.6 (numeric range DoS, was >=5.0.5)\n- webpack-dev