/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisjwalk-bot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrisjwalk/angular-cli-netcore-ngrx-starter/commits/8ca31c7dc289b3907630721096fcf8a34b9a9811/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-09T20:14:36Z","email":"268224883+chrisjwalk-bot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"chrisjwalk-bot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-09T20:14:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: update about page to demo Analog content feature, add nav link (#151)\n\n* feat: migrate Angular app to Analog.js + VitePWA (Phase 1, closes #147)\n\n- Replace @angular/build:application with @analogjs/platform:vite executor\n- Replace ngsw service worker with vite-plugin-pwa (VitePWA)\n- Migrate sw-update.store to use virtual:pwa-register from vite-plugin-pwa\n- Migrate home page from ngx-markdown to @analogjs/content MarkdownComponent\n- Add /about route with markdown content page\n- Remove SSR scaffold files generated by Analog migration\n- Add vite-plugin-pwa/client and vite/client types to tsconfig files\n- Add Shiki bash/shell/yaml language support for code block highlighting\n- Fix todo lib vite config to extend baseConfig (includes virtualPwaRegisterStub)\n- Update integration and unit tests to remove @angular/service-worker deps\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: add front-matter dep and fix CSS @import order for e2e\n\n- Install front-matter as direct workspace dep (pnpm strict isolation\n  prevented @analogjs/content from resolving its transitive dep, causing\n  ''does not provide an export named default'' page error)\n- Move @import ''./_tokens.css'' before @plugin/@source in styles.css\n  (PostCSS requires @import to precede all other at-rules)\n- Add front-matter to optimizeDeps.include so Vite pre-bundles it from CJS\n\nFixes all 32 e2e tests (30 were failing)\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: e2e backend integration, Vite proxy conflict, and CI output path\n\n- Fix port collision by splitting playwright webServer into separate API\n  and frontend entries; add serve-e2e target without api:serve dependency\n- Fix API health check URL to use HTTP (dev HTTPS redirect is now prod-only)\n- Fix Vite proxy conflict: set Analog.js apiPrefix to ''_analog'' so its\n  Nitro dev server no longer intercepts /api requests before the proxy\n- Switch Vite proxy target from https://localhost:60254 to http://localhost:60253\n  (avoids HTTPS cert issues in dev; redirect now production-only)\n- Add weather forecast API integration e2e test (table-row visibility)\n- Add home.e2e.spec.ts and about.e2e.spec.ts for Analog.js content pages\n- Fix CI/deploy output path: browser/ -> client/ (Analog.js default)\n  Updates preview.yml, deploy.yml comment, and Program.cs PhysicalFileProvider\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: only serve static SPA files and UseSpa in production\n\nIn development, Vite serves the SPA so PhysicalFileProvider and UseSpa\nshould not run — attempting to do so causes DirectoryNotFoundException\nsince the dist output does not exist during local development.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: restore preview build configuration for environment file replacement\n\nThe Analog migration dropped the ''preview'' configuration from project.json.\nWithout it, ''nx build web-app --configuration preview'' didn''t pass mode:preview\nto Vite, so the fileReplacements in vite.config.ts (swapping environment.ts\nwith environment.preview.ts) never ran. Preview deployments to Azure SWA had\nan empty apiBaseUrl and all /api calls stayed on the SWA host with no backend.\n\nAdding ''preview'': { mode: ''preview'' } restores the environment swap, causing\nthe apiBaseUrlInterceptor to prepend the production App Service URL for all\n/api requests in preview builds.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: use production mode for preview build to enable Angular optimizer\n\nUsing mode: ''preview'' in the Vite build configuration prevented the\nAngular build optimizer (@analogjs/vite-plugin-angular) from replacing\nngDevMode with false, leaving 12 dev-mode code paths in the bundle.\nThis caused the app to fail to render in the Azure SWA preview environment.\n\nFix:\n- Set mode: ''production'' in project.json preview configuration so Vite\n  sets NODE_ENV=production, enabling the Angular optimizer correctly\n- Use process.env[''NX_TASK_TARGET_CONFIGURATION''] === ''preview'' in\n  vite.config.ts to detect preview builds for file replacements instead\n  of relying on the Vite mode parameter\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: update about page to demo Analog content feature, add nav link (closes #150)\n\n- Rewrite about.md to explain and demonstrate the Analog.js content\n  feature (injectContent, frontmatter, TOC, Shiki highlighting,\n  injectContentFiles, slug routing, Mermaid diagrams)\n- Update About component to use toSignal, display frontmatter attributes\n  as a hero header, render content.toc as an ''On this page'' nav,\n  and show injectContentFiles() results in a footer panel\n- Install mermaid and enable it via withMarkdownRenderer({ loadMermaid })\n- Configure Shiki to skipLangs: [''mermaid''] so Mermaid blocks use the\n  runtime SVG renderer\n- Add About link to NAV_LINKS (toolbar + sidenav)\n- Add Analog.js to README/home.md features and tech stack sections\n- Update e2e specs to match new about page structure\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(about): sticky TOC sidebar, wider layout, working anchor links\n\n- Add withInMemoryScrolling({ anchorScrolling: ''enabled'' }) to router\n  so plain href=\"#id\" fragment links work natively (matches Analog blog-app pattern)\n- Move TOC from inline above content to a sticky right sidebar (hidden below xl:)\n- Sticky position accounts for toolbar height via calc(--mat-toolbar-standard-height + 1.5rem)\n- Widen page from max-w-3xl to max-w-6xl with two-column flex layout\n- Remove manual scrollTo/DOCUMENT workaround (no longer needed)\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(content): working TOC scroll, sticky sidebar, rename about→content\n\nRoot cause of broken links and sticky: <main id=\"main-content\" class=\"overflow-auto\">\nis the scroll container, not window. Angular''s anchorScrolling targets window only.\n\n- Restore scrollIntoView() click handler (scrolls the correct container)\n- Use href=\"javascript:void(0)\" + (click) to avoid router interception\n- Fix sticky top: top-8 instead of toolbar calc (main already starts below toolbar)\n- Rename route /about → /content, files about.* → content.*, class About → Content\n- Update nav-links label/hint/routerLink, app.routes.ts, e2e spec\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(content): rename content.md back to about.md to avoid Analog API conflict\n\nAnalog''s content API is served at /_analog/content/... so naming the file\ncontent.md caused a circular path conflict (/_analog/content/content).\nThe route /content and nav label can differ from the internal filename.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(content): move aria-label to nav element for e2e test compatibility\n\ngetByRole(''navigation'', { name: /on this page/i }) looks for aria-label\non the <nav> element itself, not the parent <aside>.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(content): ssr guard for mermaid, diagram syntax fixes, sticky toc\n\n  during server-side rendering (causes white screen without this)\n- Replace \\n with <br/> in mermaid node labels (unsupported escape)\n- Remove quoted subgraph titles and [slug] brackets that caused\n  mermaid parse failures\n- Remove flex items-start so aside stretches to full container height,\n  allowing position:sticky to work correctly on the TOC nav\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(content): active section tracking in toc via IntersectionObserver\n\n- Uses IntersectionObserver with root: main#main-content (the scroll\n  container) and rootMargin: ''0px 0px -75% 0px'' to activate a heading\n  when it enters the top 25% of the viewport\n- activeId signal drives the active link state; also set immediately\n  on click for snappy UX during the smooth-scroll animation\n- Active TOC entry shows text-primary + font-medium + primary left\n  border; inactive entries show a 2px transparent border that reveals\n  the grey track line on the <ul>\n- SSR guard (typeof IntersectionObserver === ''undefined'') prevents\n  errors during server-side rendering\n- DestroyRef cleans up the observer when the component is destroyed\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(content): simplify mermaid diagrams to avoid html-in-pre rendering bug\n\n<br/> tags inside <pre class=\"mermaid\"> are rendered as real HTML line\nbreaks by the browser before mermaid parses the text content. This\nsplits node labels across lines causing a syntax error. Remove all\nspecial html and special chars from node labels.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* test(e2e): add robust content page tests\n\nCovers every regression found during development:\n- No ''No Content Found'' error (filename/API conflict regression)\n- No blank page on load (SSR mermaid crash regression)\n- Mermaid diagrams render as SVG elements\n- No mermaid syntax errors in rendered output\n- Clicking a TOC link immediately highlights it (activeId set on click)\n- Scrolling the page updates the active TOC link via IntersectionObserver\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore: update all packages to latest\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"acc478e9ad25a410a47a3ca0ba99d91e31b262f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrisjwalk/angular-cli-netcore-ngrx-starter/git/trees/acc478e9ad25a410a47a3ca0ba99d91e31b262f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrisjwalk/angular-cli-netcore-ngrx-starter/git/commits/8ca31c7dc289b3907630721096fcf8a34b9a9811","verification":{"payload":"tree acc478e9ad25a410a47a3ca0ba99d91e31b262f7\nparent f5e41b94fbfffbb86f14dabbf272022dbd582ae6\nauthor chrisjwalk-bot <268224883+chrisjwalk-bot@users.noreply.github.com> 1778357676 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778357676 -0400\n\nfeat: update about page to demo Analog content feature, add nav link (#151)\n\n* feat: migrate Angular app to Analog.js + VitePWA (Phase 1, closes #147)\n\n- Replace @angular/build:application with @analogjs/platform:vite executor\n- Replace ngsw service worker with vite-plugin-pwa (VitePWA)\n- Migrate sw-update.store to use virtual:pwa-register from vite-plugin-pwa\n- Migrate home page from ngx-markdown to @analogjs/content MarkdownComponent\n- Add /about route with markdown content page\n- Remove SSR scaffold files generated by Analog migration\n- Add vite-plugin-pwa/client and vite/client types to tsconfig files\n- Add Shiki bash/shell/yaml language support for code block highlighting\n- Fix todo lib vite config to extend baseConfig (includes virtualPwaRegisterStub)\n- Update integration and unit tests to remove @angular/service-worker deps\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: add front-matter dep and fix CSS @import order for e2e\n\n- Install front-matter as direct workspace dep (pnpm strict isolation\n  prevented @analogjs/content from resolving its transitive dep, causing\n  ''does not provide an export named default'' page error)\n- Move @import ''./_tokens.css'' before @plugin/@source in styles.css\n  (PostCSS requires @import to precede all other at-rules)\n- Add front-matter to optimizeDeps.include so Vite pre-bundles it from CJS\n\nFixes all 32 e2e tests (30 were failing)\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: e2e backend integration, Vite proxy conflict, and CI output path\n\n- Fix port collision by splitting playwright webServer into separate API\n  and frontend entries; add serve-e2e target without api:serve dependency\n- Fix API health check URL to use HTTP (dev HTTPS redirect is now prod-only)\n- Fix Vite proxy conflict: set Analog.js apiPrefix to ''_analog'' so its\n  Nitro dev server no longer intercepts /api requests before the proxy\n- Switch Vite proxy target from https://localhost:60254 to http://localhost:60253\n  (avoids HTTPS cert issues in dev; redirect now production-only)\n- Add weather forecast API integration e2e test (table-row visibility)\n- Add home.e2e.spec.ts and about.e2e.spec.ts for Analog.js content pages\n- Fix CI/deploy output path: browser/ -> client/ (Analog.js default)\n  Updates preview.yml, deploy.yml comment, and Program.cs PhysicalFileProvider\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: only serve static SPA files and UseSpa in production\n\nIn development, Vite serves the SPA so PhysicalFileProvider and UseSpa\nshould not run — attempting to do so causes DirectoryNotFoundException\nsince the dist output does not exist during local development.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: restore preview build configuration for environment file replacement\n\nThe Analog migration dropped the ''preview'' configuration from project.json.\nWithout it, ''nx build web-app --configuration preview'' didn''t pass mode:preview\nto Vite, so the fileReplacements in vite.config.ts (swapping environment.ts\nwith environment.preview.ts) never ran. Preview deployments to Azure SWA had\nan empty apiBaseUrl and all /api calls stayed on the SWA host with no backend.\n\nAdding ''preview'': { mode: ''preview'' } restores the environment swap, causing\nthe apiBaseUrlInterceptor to prepend the production App Service URL for all\n/api requests in preview builds.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: use production mode for preview build to enable Angular optimizer\n\nUsing mode: ''preview'' in the Vite build configuration prevented the\nAngular build optimizer (@analogjs/vite-plugin-angular) from replacing\nngDevMode with false, leaving 12 dev-mode code paths in the bundle.\nThis caused the app to fail to render in the Azure SWA preview environment.\n\nFix:\n- Set mode: ''production'' in project.json preview configuration so Vite\n  sets NODE_ENV=production, enabling the Angular optimizer correctly\n- Use process.env[''NX_TASK_TARGET_CONFIGURATION''] === ''preview'' in\n  vite.config.ts to detect preview builds for file replacements instead\n  of relying on the Vite mode parameter\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: update about page to demo Analog content feature, add nav link (closes #150)\n\n- Rewrite about.md to explain and demonstrate the Analog.js content\n  feature (injectContent, frontmatter, TOC, Shiki highlighting,\n  injectContentFiles, slug routing, Mermaid diagrams)\n- Update About component to use toSignal, display frontmatter attributes\n  as a hero header, render content.toc as an ''On this page'' nav,\n  and show injectContentFiles() results in a footer panel\n- Install mermaid and enable it via withMarkdownRenderer({ loadMermaid })\n- Configure Shiki to skipLangs: [''mermaid''] so Mermaid blocks use the\n  runtime SVG renderer\n- Add About link to NAV_LINKS (toolbar + sidenav)\n- Add Analog.js to README/home.md features and tech stack sections\n- Update e2e specs to match new about page structure\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(about): sticky TOC sidebar, wider layout, working anchor links\n\n- Add withInMemoryScrolling({ anchorScrolling: ''enabled'' }) to router\n  so plain href=\"#id\" fragment links work natively (matches Analog blog-app pattern)\n- Move TOC from inline above content to a sticky right sidebar (hidden below xl:)\n- Sticky position accounts for toolbar height via calc(--mat-toolbar-standard-height + 1.5rem)\n- Widen page from max-w-3xl to max-w-6xl with two-column flex layout\n- Remove manual scrollTo/DOCUMENT workaround (no longer needed)\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(content): working TOC scroll, sticky sidebar, rename about→content\n\nRoot cause of broken links and sticky: <main id=\"main-content\" class=\"overflow-auto\">\nis the scroll container, not window. Angular''s anchorScrolling targets window only.\n\n- Restore scrollIntoView() click handler (scrolls the correct container)\n- Use href=\"javascript:void(0)\" + (click) to avoid router interception\n- Fix sticky top: top-8 instead of toolbar calc (main already starts below toolbar)\n- Rename route /about → /content, files about.* → content.*, class About → Content\n- Update nav-links label/hint/routerLink, app.routes.ts, e2e spec\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(content): rename content.md back to about.md to avoid Analog API conflict\n\nAnalog''s content API is served at /_analog/content/... so naming the file\ncontent.md caused a circular path conflict (/_analog/content/content).\nThe route /content and nav label can differ from the internal filename.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(content): move aria-label to nav element for e2e test compatibility\n\ngetByRole(''navigation'', { name: /on this page/i }) looks for aria-label\non the <nav> element itself, not the parent <aside>.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(content): ssr guard for mermaid, diagram syntax fixes, sticky toc\n\n  during server-side rendering (causes white screen without this)\n- Replace \\n with <br/> in mermaid node labels (unsupported escape)\n- Remove quoted subgraph titles and [slug] brackets that caused\n  mermaid parse failures\n- Remove flex items-start so aside stretches to full container height,\n  allowing position:sticky to work correctly on the TOC nav\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(content): active section tracking in toc via IntersectionObserver\n\n- Uses IntersectionObserver with root: main#main-content (the scroll\n  container) and rootMargin: ''0px 0px -75% 0px'' to activate a heading\n  when it enters the top 25% of the viewport\n- activeId signal drives the active link state; also set immediately\n  on click for snappy UX during the smooth-scroll animation\n- Active TOC entry shows text-primary + font-medium + primary left\n  border; inactive entries show a 2px transparent border that reveals\n  the grey track line on the <ul>\n- SSR guard (typeof IntersectionObserver === ''undefined'') prevents\n  errors during server-side rendering\n- DestroyRef cleans up the observer when the component is destroyed\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(content): simplify mermaid diagrams to avoid html-in-pre rendering bug\n\n<br/> tags inside <pre class=\"mermaid\"> are rendered as real HTML line\nbreaks by the browser before mermaid parses the text content. This\nsplits node labels across lines causing a syntax error. Remove all\nspecial html and special chars from node labels.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* test(e2e): add robust content page tests\n\nCovers every regression found during development:\n- No ''No Content Found'' error (filename/API conflict regression)\n- No blank page on load (SSR mermaid crash regression)\n- Mermaid diagrams render as SVG elements\n- No mermaid syntax errors in rendered output\n- Clicking a TOC link immediately highlights it (activeId set on click)\n- Scrolling the page updates the active TOC link via IntersectionObserver\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore: update all packages to latest\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/5WsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKgIQAFJDB0K5xy7hGzGcBMRohAYs\nPMLM7YAAvKC2SKkzzQYj7UtaLPCuMY5zWW4NbljWKJLFsFN1cSaPPAfX5iXOinLC\nO3fuqbRuDrp1gkY9d7h5mpB7AerSDEX301dPdESRFPrTIXfN1sS2NJBXIWswR8Qg\nay/udCloM+z1tcTUNu73NShl9cIQDVdhwD40axE9MoLDhs+pGipwb6V8ytHJQ67w\no7vsCVPng08EqJAynU9zuwpFBMBUS7NflkVhdnYINglNBl5orz//VOU87vcW/Avz\nB0znEFsNjY/yGlmdZGb3IoIjxVMdNbDx9b5GWy2HHsGxhd4zyMS6j2LuHKO1Gkyw\nCpJXMiIk4K8KqY462YV6jE3MGMoq8WnG3EvitD+ZQK+8w8ox6IqiUiD4zIv/Z6Gj\n2/hWY0IYR0tUcnw1zNNiPglSfdEfTag3VKeSMLw+OdnXbLneQR5vOiGG8MZO9wwb\n7LGA5cCYX6Sm3pXKDGfw5wFoedduPEFMU1iQUlIX0L25lDmzyp0Vul2XKAHbJsln\nZa/6BoG+Cqo3Qq1+8xKMAcm1+1AuRWxzsAoEvGxaa8mC+lC0BmOK/GV5jMoMqM9h\njXHDxVduXtUoOhsh/iinkjTKCNbxsnJaG3Nw2ka9Sk0g0xqIO9TO6J6EIKqzSLyF\nw/1MtJzxvWrm2vM1GG5a\n=zksw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-09T20:14:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_ur