 Explains that the default `String` formatter produces scientific\nnotation for large values, breaking `toDecimal` with libraries like\nbig.js at high precision (scale >= 22)\n- Shows how to provide a custom formatter using `toFixed()` and pass it\nto `createDinero`\n\nFixes #716\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a0dd0930cc3a020dba02dffcf1e5e7703f10ec35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dinerojs/dinero.js/git/trees/a0dd0930cc3a020dba02dffcf1e5e7703f10ec35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dinerojs/dinero.js/git/commits/9e5b513962344d73dc99c72e94cc385a77f17e58","verification":{"payload":"tree a0dd0930cc3a020dba02dffcf1e5e7703f10ec35\nparent 2536a1fb8cfbb5ff9694886168ebe74b57281505\nauthor Sarah Dayan <5370675+sarahdayan@users.noreply.github.com> 1770481664 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1770481664 +0100\n\ndocs: document custom formatter requirement for third-party amount types (#823)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Add a \"Providing a custom formatter\" subsection to the precision and\nlarge numbers guide\n- Explains that the default `String` formatter produces scientific\nnotation for large values, breaking `toDecimal` with libraries like\nbig.js at high precision (scale >= 22)\n- Shows how to provide a custom formatter using `toFixed()` and pass it\nto `createDinero`\n\nFixes #716\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJph2gACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoVQQAKI/pxRXE8aHmi6qC68g47E9\nS6DVFVXZM0GItCaKGMDYVJ4xGgnzHA38Jce7Qx/5QgZD7Rykapua5dqakjndi/4B\n6klDI44goHbA1tfCsC/3So2vmuHwkFKgGnmrp0dYeRKxkeMwkIAzsWhneJJePGBM\nQ/oQm+3gbdG+Tn6iAqvw/Mi3g/+/jLmTpM+mvVADHXl5VRiYOUkLlI2YLxnDn9J5\nWjVd4PCzzitFIRYFDpAtIOXP9JSHDwm2Ntsms/YP8Z2LSUs0eqgzcgv76lubsTCG\nsU4O8cMUu1K5DETGbFQC8JyyD1/JBFtdCelELYmFXAA6O1weyehXwjxg8QK+dBAi\n9/5oQNOV6OwHiwFjNNmMIpT5LWLpuuQTTJDnVuB+Yp9kRPbYoG7YTmCdUQAfqz6b\nhr8rKka6lLEVSPc5luDx8GZKEpYHe7SPpHMCkYIE1iD1XFrGmBf2sCsuGAE4KL